WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.516
The Design phase turns analysis into a learning plan.

00:00:03.516 --> 00:00:07.312
This is where course creators define learning objectives, performance outcomes,

00:00:07.312 --> 00:00:10.728
module sequence, instructional strategy, examples, practice opportunities, assessment approach,

00:00:10.728 --> 00:00:13.385
narration plan, visual direction, and accessibility expectations.

00:00:13.385 --> 00:00:17.940
The design should explain how the course will help learners move from

00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:19.838
current performance to desired performance.

00:00:19.838 --> 00:00:23.254
Learning objectives should be specific enough to guide development.

00:00:23.254 --> 00:00:29.328
A vague objective such as understand the policy is hard to teach and hard to assess.

00:00:29.328 --> 00:00:34.642
A stronger objective describes what learners will be able to identify, choose, apply, compare,

00:00:34.642 --> 00:00:35.781
perform, or explain.

00:00:35.781 --> 00:00:38.438
The objective becomes a filter for content:

00:00:38.438 --> 00:00:41.474
if a detail does not support the objective,

00:00:41.474 --> 00:00:46.029
it may belong in a reference document instead of the main course.

00:00:46.029 --> 00:00:47.168
Course structure matters.

00:00:47.168 --> 00:00:52.482
Modules should build in a logical order, usually from context to concepts to application.

00:00:52.482 --> 00:00:54.380
Examples make abstract content concrete.

00:00:54.380 --> 00:00:59.315
Practice gives learners a chance to use the information before the final assessment.

00:00:59.315 --> 00:01:03.490
Assessments should measure the same knowledge or decisions the course teaches.

00:01:03.490 --> 00:01:07.286
Alignment is the core design discipline: objectives, content, practice, media,

00:01:07.286 --> 00:01:10.322
and assessment should point in the same direction.

00:01:10.322 --> 00:01:13.739
Storyboards make the design visible before production becomes expensive.

00:01:13.739 --> 00:01:17.914
A storyboard can show screen flow, narration, visual ideas, interactions, feedback,

00:01:17.914 --> 00:01:19.053
and quiz alignment.

00:01:19.053 --> 00:01:23.228
It gives stakeholders something to review before the team records audio,

00:01:23.228 --> 00:01:25.885
builds complex interactions, or creates final media.

00:01:25.885 --> 00:01:27.783
A storyboard is not busywork;

00:01:27.783 --> 00:01:33.097
it is a way to catch problems while they are still cheap to fix.

00:01:33.097 --> 00:01:36.893
Accessibility should be planned here, not added at the end.

00:01:36.893 --> 00:01:41.068
Decisions about captions, transcripts, keyboard navigation, alt text, reading order, contrast,

00:01:41.068 --> 00:01:44.105
plain language, and media alternatives all affect design.

00:01:44.105 --> 00:01:48.660
A strong design phase makes the learner experience clearer before development begins.
